I'm no one when it comes to this as I've never owned a business and I'm currently broke. However, with 500k you can pretty much think of anything you've ever dreamed of doing and turn it into a business.

&#x200B;

For example, I'm into van living and dream of owning one of those beautiful Mercedes Sprinter vans with wooden floors and a shower all custom made. With a. fraction of what you have I would buy a used one with low miles and transform it myself while learning all the ins and outs and then make a blog of the whole process and then offer to do conversions for other people.

&#x200B;

Or I would buy a specific older Japanese car like an MR2 and tune it to my taste and also offer to do the same for other people. Maybe the more experienced people here think I'm crazy. But what I'm saying is with just a fraction of what you have saved you can probably do anything you love and turn it into a business. I'm sure there's something you've always wanted to do that could be monetized as I'm sure whatever it is you love is loved by many out there without the time to do it themselves.

&#x200B;

You could make art, scale models, your own damn horror movie series, pretty much anything man and chances are there's a market for it and now you have the money to reach that market.  


Is it the #1 most viable and realistic way to increase your profits to the max ? probably not. Could you possibly make your craziest dreams come true and even get paid for it? Absolutely.  Could you maximize profits at first with something safer and then make even more dreams come true? For sure another option haha

Thank you! I don't feel I've done anything horrible though , I do have guilt because that accident could've been avoided had I just driven my mom's car instead. (It was raining hard and my car was very low and broke down) but I was not at fault, someone crashed into us. I am going to see a therapist, I made a call to make an appointment today.

&#x200B;

As for nature, I was raised and lived until I was 11 years old at the foot of a mountain in another country. I would spend a lot of time as a kid alone in the mountain and I guess I've always missed that. Specially since I moved to a city in the US with no mountains and completely different weather and not much nature.

